  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">R4D Sankore West Africa project 300704-414</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sankore programme is structured across three interconnected workstreams designed to strengthen innovation systems in Ghana and Nigeria while maximising collaboration and learning. First, R4D will support FMIST and MESTI to commercialise innovations in priority sectors (agriculture and energy) through a phased, &#x201c;learning by doing&#x201d; approach&#x2014;identifying demand, sourcing innovations, assessing commercialisation needs, and implementing tailored support strategies. Second, ACET will improve policy and regulatory environments by analysing existing frameworks, developing long-term transformation roadmaps, prioritising key reform &#x201c;sticky issues,&#x201d; and engaging stakeholders across government, academia, and the private sector. Third, R4D will establish a demand-driven Helpdesk (WATIH) for FCDO staff, providing rapid, tailored technical support, expert advice, and resources for innovation-related projects. Together, these workstreams are integrated through shared governance, cross-learning, and coordinated activities to enhance efficiency, strengthen ecosystems, and drive sustainable innovation outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
